sx1255-multimode (1.0.0~rc5-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * FM/SVXLink: de-emphasis and pre-emphasis moved to SVXLink ([Rx1]
    DEEMPHASIS=1, [Tx1] PREEMPHASIS=1), which is what those settings are
    for when the audio comes straight from the discriminator and the FM
    modulator is driven directly.  The multimode sets rx_deemph_us and
    tx_preemph_us to 0, which turns both filters into a plain passthrough;
    non-zero values still apply them in the multimode (local backend).

 -- Karel Kadlec (OK1LBC) <xkk@post.cz>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0000

sx1255-multimode (1.0.0~rc5-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * FM: the RX audio forwarded to SVXLink is no longer filtered.  The CTCSS
    notch bank (20 notches at n x 88.5 Hz across the whole voice band) was
    audibly degrading the demodulated audio; the tone now passes through and
    SVXLink handles it.  CTCSS detection in the multimode is unchanged.

 -- Karel Kadlec (OK1LBC) <xkk@post.cz>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000

sx1255-multimode (1.0.0~rc5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * M17 packet reception no longer loses packets: the decoder re-synchronizes
    on every valid LSF, multi-frame packets are reassembled by frame number,
    the synchronizer buffer survives session start/stop, the end marker only
    ends a synchronized transmission and the last frame of a packet is found
    without the following sync word.
  * M17 keeps decoding while another mode owns the session (FM/D-Star hang
    time), and network packets wait in a queue instead of being dropped.
  * Transmit arbitration separates data from audio: a packet is no longer
    refused because the network audio source is another mode.
  * Packet statistics and message logging in the log and the dashboard.

 -- Karel Kadlec (OK1LBC) <xkk@post.cz>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000

